SauronID — licence map
======================

This repository is not under a single licence. Which terms apply depends on
which component you are looking at, because the clients are meant to be free,
the proofs must be inspectable to be worth anything, and the gateway is the
product.

Apache License 2.0 — full text in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0
----------------------------------------------------

    agentic/                TypeScript SDK
    clients/python/         Python SDK
    clients/go/             Go SDK
    mcp-server/             MCP server
    transparent-zk/         RISC Zero guests, journal types, customer verifier

These are deliberately open. The SDKs and the MCP server are thin clients: they
hold no keys, evaluate no policy and enforce nothing, and they are inert without
a gateway to talk to. transparent-zk must be open for a different reason — a
customer has to rebuild the guest programs from source to reproduce the image IDs
committed in every proof. A proof whose program nobody can inspect is not
evidence.

Business Source License 1.1 — full text in LICENSE-BUSL-1.1
------------------------------------------------------------

    core/                   the authorization gateway
    dashboard/              the operator console

Read it, build it, modify it, run it in development — always, by anyone, at no
cost. **Production use is free while your organisation's annual revenue is below
EUR 1,000,000**, and requires a commercial licence above that. Offering it to
third parties as a hosted or managed service is not permitted at any size.

On 2030-08-16 these components become Apache-2.0 automatically. That date is
fixed and does not move.

The reasoning, since a licence that is not understood is not respected: a
security gateway you cannot read is a gateway you have to take on trust, which
is the opposite of what this project claims to offer. So the source is public.
But the work is funded by the organisations large enough to need it, so those
organisations pay. Small teams and evaluators cost nothing to serve and are
welcome.

Everything else
---------------

    examples/, redteam/, scripts/, deploy/, docs/, schemas/, site/, branding/,
    contracts/, migrations/, zkp/

Supporting material for the above. Not separately licensed: treat it as
Apache-2.0 where it accompanies an Apache-2.0 component, and as BUSL-1.1 where
it accompanies the gateway. `branding/` is excluded — see Trademarks.

Trademarks
----------

No licence is granted to any SauronID name, wordmark, eye logo, or brand asset
under `branding/`. Neither the Apache grant nor the BUSL grant conveys trademark
rights: BUSL says so explicitly, and Apache-2.0 section 6 does the same. You may
run and modify the software; you may not distribute it under our name.

